    {
      "@id": "#assertion-comparator-interpretation",
      "@type": "ftro:Assertion",
      "name": "Which of two documented physical interpretations does the comparator output carry?",
      "ftro:subject": {
        "@id": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.17107693"
      },
      "ftro:evidence_state": "unresolved",
      "ftro:contestation_state": "none",
      "ftro:competing_readings": [
        {
          "ftro:reading": "Ref = A: Delta = rho-tilde(B,A), frequency of B referenced to A",
          "ftro:reference_oscillator": "oscillator A"
        },
        {
          "ftro:reading": "Ref = local RF: Delta = rho-tilde(B,x) - rho-tilde(A,x)",
          "ftro:reference_oscillator": "an unnamed local RF reference x"
        }
      ],
      "ftro:note": "All 12 comparisons use rho0 = nu0B/nu0A and sB = nu0B, which matches TWO rows of the pinned format's examples table differing only by ref_osc. The two have different reference oscillators and therefore different time-tag ancestry. Both readings are retained; neither is selected. FTRO-DEF-004.",
